title: What a row was for is in its transcript only if the first request says it.
pid: 154f454d-f115-44d1-aa09-7a8e18d6713c
body: |2-
  A mind lent with the prompt 'tools/team/specialist.sh prompt' prints
  names its specialist, its mission's ID and, since 2026-11-13, the
  mission's kind (plan, reading, build or tending), and the account
  reads all three, and gives them to the subagents that mind starts.
  The kind is in no transcript older than that, so 'mission_kind' is
  empty there, and a kind must still be guessed for those rows. Missions Top wrote in its
  own words, like "Mario: move configs into owners' folders", name
  neither, though the subagent's description often names the specialist.
  So sums by specialist are whole only if every mission is lent through
  'specialist.sh prompt'.
  A pacer session gets no generated title, unlike an interactive one;
  what it did is only in the pacer's log, whose "session STAMP starts"
  time is within two seconds of the row's 'began'.
